"""The Colab notebooks are generated by ``scripts/build_notebooks.py`` and committed.

These tests regenerate them into a temporary directory, check that every notebook is a
valid nbformat v4 document with at least six cells, that every code cell compiles, that
the shared skeleton (setup / Drive / configuration / stage run / summary) is present, and
that the committed notebooks are identical to the regenerated ones (normalised JSON:
outputs and execution counts ignored) so that they can never drift from the generator.

The stage G-L notebooks (06-11) must additionally carry the pre-registration paragraph,
the substage report and the stage-specific keyword arguments of their ``run()``.

Notebook 12 (``12_trace_source``, the A100 run of the stage-L trace source) has its own
skeleton test: setup / Drive / configuration / runner / summary as in 00-11, every
pipeline step (download, serialize, hash-split vocabulary with held-out OOV, bf16 training
with checkpoints and resume, evaluation against unigram / bigram / untrained, controlled
probes, length-residualised alignment, stage L with ``trace:<model_dir>``), the cost
table and the frozen feature; every ``python -m lsne.chain.cli`` option the notebook
passes must exist in the parser of ``lsne.chain.cli``.  Its headless smoke execution on
the Xatu fixture is marked ``slow``.  The committed notebooks must also be byte-identical
to the generator output.

Notebook 13 (``13_prereg_evaluation``, CPU runtime without accelerator metadata) has its own
tests: the skeleton (header, the ``LSNE_B`` shortcut note, the run roots asked for in the
configuration cell, the evaluation through ``lsne.prereg_eval``), the CLI equivalent (only
options of ``python -m lsne.prereg_eval``) and a headless execution on a tiny synthetic run
root (no model, so it is not marked ``slow``; skipped without a Jupyter kernel).

Notebook 14 (``14_token_control``, the A100 control run of the injection-site language,
PREREGISTRATION 6.11) has its own tests: the skeleton and defaults (main run of account A,
the ``LSNE_B`` shortcut only when it is missing, the own root ``runs_ctl``, ``REUSE = False``),
the CLI call (only options of ``python -m lsne.cli run``, the control flags included), its
cells executed in this process on synthetic runs (the stops with a German message: main run
missing, not ok, without its bank, a foreign run in the control directory, no GPU; the
descriptive check and the summary; nothing is written below ``RUNS_ROOT``) and, marked
``slow``, a headless execution in smoke mode that runs the control through the CLI against a
main run built here with pythia-14m.

``test_notebook_runs_headless_in_smoke_mode`` (marked ``slow``) executes notebooks 00 and
06 with ``SMOKE = True`` (pythia-14m, DEV01) through nbclient inside this checkout: every
cell must run without an uncaught error, the stage manifest must say ``ok`` and the
summary json / figures must be written below ``$LSNE_RUNS``.  It is skipped when no
Jupyter kernel can be started.
"""
